# Hub CI/CD

This managed guide describes the minimum workflow for this ontology hub. See `CONTRIBUTING.md` for
authoring and review conventions.

## Branching

- `main` is protected and is the only long-lived branch.
- Use short-lived `model/*`, `import/*`, `fix/*`, or `upgrade/*` branches.
- DEV, UAT, and PROD are deployment targets, not Git branches.
- Never hand-edit compiler-owned files under `ontology-hub-publish/`.

## Pull-request checks

From `ontology-hub/`, run the focused checks for every changed domain:

```powershell
uv sync --locked
uv run kairos-ontology compile <domain> --check --format json
uv run kairos-ontology compile <domain> --explain --format json
uv run kairos-ontology compile <domain> --emit --confirm-emit
```

The pull request must include any release-relevant generated diff required by repository policy.
CI must regenerate the same output and fail on drift. A green result proves compilation and
structural validation; it does not replace a real downstream dbt build.

## Release

1. Merge the reviewed change to `main`.
2. Tag the exact validated commit.
3. Let `.github/workflows/release-projections.yml` validate and publish the projection artifacts.
4. Record the full 40-character hub commit SHA for dataplatform adoption.

A release tag is a readable label. The dataplatform dependency must use the full commit SHA.

### Power BI release artifact

When Gold Power BI output is configured, the same release also publishes
`powerbi-semantic-model.zip`. It contains the first generated `SemanticModel` and `Report`
versions from the same hub commit.

The release workflow performs all wrapper generation and TMDL normalization before validating
PBIP/report structure, TMDL, DAX, relationships, and generated security metadata. Release evidence
records the hub SHA and archive SHA-256. Gold configuration without both expected item types fails
the release.

The generated report is a deployable starting point, not business signoff. Change compiler-owned
report or semantic-model output in the hub inputs and regenerate it; never patch the archive.

## Hotfix

Create the hub hotfix from the hub SHA used by PROD, publish a new release, and adopt its new SHA in
the dataplatform. Then forward-port the same fix and regression test onto a branch from current hub
`main`, using cherry-pick when it applies cleanly; do not merge the old release history wholesale
into `main`.

## Managed files

Adopt a newer managed guide and toolkit release in an isolated upgrade PR:

```powershell
uv run kairos-ontology update --upgrade
# On Windows, wait for the detached managed-file refresh to finish.
uv run kairos-ontology update --check
```

If the toolkit pin is already current, run `uv run kairos-ontology update` without `--upgrade`;
plain `update` completes synchronously. Only a version-changing Windows `update --upgrade` requires
checking `.kairos/upgrade-refresh.log`. Review all managed, lock, and generated consequences before
merging.
